- globals.css: alle Touch-Target-Regeln 44px -> 48px (button, input/textarea/select, nav a,
  footer summary/nav a, icon-button, text-button, download-link, slot, send-button 48x48,
  mobile-nav summary, account-control/account-link). Font-Clamps unberuehrt.
- Komponenten-CSS 44px -> 48px: PartnerRequestForm, ShopPanel, WorkshopDirectory,
  WorkspaceStatusPanel, WorkspaceRebuild (account-link/text-button/checkbox-label/
  panel-pascal-link/chat-modes), PresenterEditorial (next-step/guide-summary).
- PublicOrientationChat .orientation-starter 40px -> var(--layout-control-size) (token 48px).
- Bewusster Opt-out .compact-touch (44px) + native checkbox/radio (20px in >=48px-Zeilen) bleiben,
  dokumentiert. Tokens --target-min/--layout-control-size waren bereits 48px.
- Evidenz real neu gemessen (echte Chromium-Laeufe, kein Hash-Patch als Nachweis):
  browser-critical (detail-browser + critical-fresh), text-spacing, shop, catalog,
  workspace-read, legal-footer vite + next (frischer Next-Build als Messbasis).
- Register chirurgisch nachgezogen: config/acceptance-coverage.json.
- Frischer Render: 0 interaktive Elemente < 48px (stale Dev-Server-Werte verworfen).
- make test = 620 OK.
